After working through that library, your suite would look less like “a simulator with extra buttons” and more like a **modular, Python-first reservoir engineering workbench**: one integrated project database, a 3D/map/plot workspace, a job-driven simulation engine, and linked modules for static modeling, well testing, production, economics, uncertainty, and reporting. The books give you the domain logic and numerical methods; the suite is the product wrapper around them.

## 1. One-sentence vision

**A web/desktop hybrid platform where an engineer can go from raw well/static/production data → QC → geological model → reservoir engineering calculations → simulation → history match → forecast → nodal/network analysis → economics → uncertainty → report, without leaving the same project and audit trail.**

